Probes run 2026-09-04 in this sandbox, via the pre-configured agent proxy.

$ curl -sS -m 8 -o /dev/null -w "HTTP %{http_code}\n" https://hex.pm
HTTP 200

$ curl -sS -m 8 -o /dev/null -w "HTTP %{http_code}\n" https://repo.hex.pm
curl: (56) CONNECT tunnel failed, response 403
[agent-proxy] repo.hex.pm:443 -- connect_rejected (organization policy)

$ curl -sS -m 8 -o /dev/null -w "HTTP %{http_code}\n" https://package.elm-lang.org
curl: (56) CONNECT tunnel failed, response 403
[agent-proxy] package.elm-lang.org:443 -- connect_rejected (organization policy)

Conclusion: the top-level hex.pm marketing site is reachable, but repo.hex.pm --
the actual package CDN mix/rebar3/hex fetch from -- is blocked by the org egress
policy, as is package.elm-lang.org (Elm's package index, needed even for a bare
`elm init` with zero dependencies). This is why the mix and rebar3 probes below
show real resolution failures rather than a completed fetch, and why no fresh
elm.json could be generated in this sandbox.
